From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: huawei_gaokun: leave the usb_0 role switch to userspace

The Huawei MateBook E Go EC always reports the connector partner type as UFP
(even when nothing is connected) and never sets the USB data capability bit, so
UCSI cannot determine the true data role of port 0. Once usb_0 is configured as
OTG with usb-role-switch, UCSI overrides the role on every connector status
update and breaks userspace role management.

Release the role switch acquired by UCSI in the update_connector hook so UCSI
continues reporting connector state, power direction, orientation, PD, and DP
alt-mode while leaving usb_0 role switching to the userspace USB HAL.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Android-specific]
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c
index 6491e48..13efcae 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_huawei_gaokun.c
@@ -238,6 +238,17 @@ static void gaokun_ucsi_update_connector(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 {
 	struct gaokun_ucsi *uec = ucsi_get_drvdata(con->ucsi);
 
+	/*
+	 * The EC reports partner type UFP in every connector status, even with
+	 * nothing attached, and never sets the USB data flag, so UCSI has no
+	 * basis for a data role. The role of usb_0 (otg on Android, for USB
+	 * device mode) is left to userspace: drop the role switch UCSI has just
+	 * looked up (only usb_0 has one), which turns its role updates into
+	 * no-ops.
+	 */
+	usb_role_switch_put(con->usb_role_sw);
+	con->usb_role_sw = NULL;
+
 	if (con->num > uec->num_ports)
 		return;
 
